{
  "root_cause": "schema_migration_regression",
  "summary": "A schema migration performed at 09:25 caused a severe degradation in database query performance starting at 09:26, leading to high query latency, increased sequential scans, and CPU usage. This in turn caused API request timeouts and increased HTTP latency and error rates, despite stable request volume.",
  "onset_ts": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z",
  "timeline": [
    {
      "statement": "A migration was applied at 09:25 that dropped idx_orders_customer_created and created idx_orders_customer.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:25:00.000Z\",\"kind\":\"migration\",\"ref\":\"0142_orders_index\",\"actor\":\"ci-bot\",\"summary\":\"drop idx_orders_customer_created; create idx_orders_customer\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "At 09:26, mean database query latency jumped dramatically from 10.7ms to 3421.3ms, with a concurrent spike in sequential scans from 5 to 560 per minute and a moderate CPU increase.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/db.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,3421.3,560,31.9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "HTTP p95 latency and error rate increased sharply starting at 09:26, while request per second remained stable, indicating the issue was not caused by increased load.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/http.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,45.61,166.88,0.037,318"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Alerts for high database CPU and API latency started firing at 09:33 and 09:35 respectively.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "alerts.jsonl",
          "line": 1,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:33:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"DbCpuHigh\",\"severity\":\"page\",\"state\":\"firing\""
        },
        {
          "source": "alerts.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:35:00.000Z\",\"name\":\"ApiLatencyP95\",\"severity\":\"page\",\"state\":\"firing\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "API logs show repeated statement timeouts after 5000ms on the /orders/history route starting shortly after 09:26, consistent with database query delays.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "logs/app.jsonl",
          "line": 699,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:26:20.000Z\",\"service\":\"api\",\"level\":\"error\",\"msg\":\"statement timeout after 5000ms\",\"req\":\"req_148121\",\"route\":\"/orders/history\""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "statement": "The timing and nature of the database performance degradation directly follow the schema migration, indicating a regression caused by the migration.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 2,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:25:00.000Z\",\"kind\":\"migration\",\"ref\":\"0142_orders_index\",\"actor\":\"ci-bot\",\"summary\":\"drop idx_orders_customer_created; create idx_orders_customer\""
        },
        {
          "source": "metrics/db.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,3421.3,560,31.9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The stable request rate rules out increased load as a cause, focusing the root cause on the database changes.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/http.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,45.61,166.88,0.037,318"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "ruled_out": [
    {
      "statement": "Bad deploy regression unrelated to the migration is unlikely because the only deploy at 09:12 was an unrelated copy change on the account page with no impact on database metrics.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "changes.jsonl",
          "line": 1,
          "quote": "\"ts\":\"2026-03-17T09:12:00.000Z\",\"kind\":\"deploy\",\"ref\":\"v2026.3.17-b4\",\"actor\":\"ci-bot\",\"summary\":\"api: unrelated copy change on the account page\""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Resource exhaustion or memory leak is unlikely as CPU usage increased moderately and did not saturate, and there is no evidence of memory issues.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/db.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,3421.3,560,31.9"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Downstream dependency failure is ruled out because the issue is localized to database query latency and sequential scans, not external services.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source": "metrics/db.csv",
          "line": 28,
          "quote": "2026-03-17T09:26:00.000Z,3421.3,560,31.9"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "action_items": [
    "Review and optimize the new idx_orders_customer index to prevent excessive sequential scans.",
    "Add pre-deployment performance testing for schema migrations to catch regressions early.",
    "Implement monitoring to detect sudden spikes in sequential scans and query latency immediately after migrations.",
    "Consider rolling back or patching the migration if performance does not improve after optimization."
  ]
}
